        "constraints": [
          "Pagination must be complete and stable before asserting unique business-number resolution. Preserve all observed request filters and principal.",
          "For record lookup, project id and taskNo. List analysis may use the separately documented list properties. Detailed address, checklist and record-only properties require the verified detail or related operation.",
          "Today requires a stated business date field; due today, assigned today and created today are not equivalent. Do not infer a schedule from lastUpdatedOn.",
          "Area uses current areaName when observed; do not silently substitute authorityName or regionName. A source DTO snapshot with authorityName differs from the current response and is not proof of that live field.",
          "A queue scope of Todo or All is not proof that tasks are assigned to the signed-in user. Personal scope needs the authorized inspector view and verified assignment filtering. Inspector display name alone is insufficient.",
          "The clock formula is defined by the source implementation; its conditions and source timezone belong to this page knowledge. The runtime arithmetic executor contains no task status codes.",
          "The generic display/order term time is not an alias for every timestamp. Ask the page-defined temporal ordering question and resolve the duplicate time display attribute to the chosen timestamp. Keep unrelated attributes, filters, date range and area ordering unchanged.",
          "Choosing a date field for a today filter does not silently select the display/order timestamp. If both are unspecified, they remain separate clarification slots. This is a reading and ordering choice, not a scheduled appointment or actual visit time.",
          "Assignment and creation timestamps use their observed ISO values for chronological ascending order; this is not a priority or risk ranking. Missing timestamps remain unknown.",
          "Delay days refers only to the documented SLA overdueDays value in this task collection. Exceeded the service level agreement uses sla.statusCode=Overdue; it must not include Remaining or Paused tasks. Descending overdue-day ordering is the explicit ordering binding, not an urgency, risk or completion score.",
          "SLA population binding must match the exact observed scope parameter. Queued, Todo, Completed and All are separate page populations; never combine counts or call Queued a personal Todo list. Select the population binding whose contextParameters matches the current authorized request, and identify that queue scope in the answer.",
          "These context bindings cover an otherwise unfiltered queue only. Any additional search, date, inspector, area or other population filter needs its own verified context; an absent, null or empty filter is not automatically interchangeable. None of these definitions authorizes switching page scope or using a manager role as proof of team membership."
        ],
        "temporalDerivations": [
          {
            "field": "overdueDays",
            "operator": "calendar_days",
            "startField": "sla.dueOn",
            "endField": "sla.completedOn",
            "endNull": "reference_time",
            "sourceTimezone": "Asia/Dubai",
            "requiresNonNull": [
              "sla.dueOn",
              "sla.statusCode"
            ],
            "nullWhen": [],
            "nullStartValue": null,
            "description": "Calendar dates in Asia/Dubai, with one recorded reference instant for an active clock. Select sla.statusCode=Overdue for current overdue tasks. Completed OnTime/Exceeded rows are not currently overdue. Null/unknown source values are not zero."
          }
        ],
